## Why This Is Asked

Candidates must handle time-decayed scoring with dynamic insert/erase and frequent top-k queries over a moving window, a realistic pattern in recommender and CDN analytics at large scale.

## Key Concepts

- Time-decayed scoring and exponential decay
- Windowed top-k queries with lazy deletions
- Maintaining running sums in a sliding window
- Trade-offs: lazy vs eager pruning, memory vs accuracy

## Code Example

```javascript
class TimeDecayStore {
  constructor(lambda) { 
    this.lambda = lambda; 
    this.map = new Map(); 
    this.heap = new MaxHeap(); 
    this.currentT = 0; 
  }

  insert(id, score, t) {
    this.map.set(id, { score, t_last: t });
    this.heap.insert({ id, decayedScore: score, t });
  }

  update(id, score, t) {
    this.map.set(id, { score, t_last: t });
    this.heap.insert({ id, decayedScore: score, t });
  }

  erase(id) {
    this.map.delete(id);
  }

  topKInLastWindow(k, t, W) {
    this.currentT = t;
    this.pruneExpired(t - W);
    const results = [];
    const temp = [];

    while (results.length < k && !this.heap.isEmpty()) {
      const item = this.heap.extractMax();
      const current = this.map.get(item.id);

      if (current) {
        const decayed = current.score * Math.exp(-this.lambda * (t - current.t_last));
        if (current.t_last >= t - W) {
          results.push({ id: item.id, decayedScore: decayed });
          temp.push({ id: item.id, decayedScore: decayed, t: current.t_last });
        }
      }
    }

    temp.forEach(item => this.heap.insert(item));
    return results;
  }

  sumScoresInWindow(t, W) {
    let sum = 0;
    for (const [id, { score, t_last }] of this.map) {
      if (t_last >= t - W) {
        sum += score * Math.exp(-this.lambda * (t - t_last));
      }
    }
    return sum;
  }

  pruneExpired(windowStart) {
    // Lazy pruning during queries
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests the ability to design a practical data structure and reason about block balancing in edit-heavy scenarios.

## Key Concepts
- **Sqrt decomposition**: Partition data into fixed-size blocks for efficient range queries
- **Per-block sums**: Enable O(1) block-level aggregation during rangeSum operations
- **Amortized balance**: Split/merge operations maintain block sizes within bounds, ensuring O(√n) amortized time per update
- **Edge-case handling**: Proper merge/split logic prevents pathological degradation

## Code Example
```javascript
class SqrtArray {
  constructor() {
    this.blocks = [];
    this.B = 2;
  }

  _getBlock(index) {
    let count = 0;
    for (const block of this.blocks) {
      if (index < count + block.length) return block;
      count += block.length;
    }
    throw new Error('Index out of bounds');
  }

  insertAt(index, value) {
    const block = this._getBlock(index);
    block.push(value);
    block.sum += value;
    if (block.length > 2 * this.B) this._split(block);
  }

  eraseAt(index) {
    const block = this._getBlock(index);
    block.splice(index, 1);
    block.sum -= value;
    if (block.length < this.B / 2) this._merge(block);
  }

  rangeSum(l, r) {
    let sum = 0;
    let count = 0;
    for (const block of this.blocks) {
      const blockStart = count;
      const blockEnd = count + block.length - 1;
      if (r < blockStart || l > blockEnd) { count += block.length; continue; }
      const start = Math.max(l, blockStart);
      const end = Math.min(r, blockEnd);
      if (start === blockStart && end === blockEnd) sum += block.sum;
      else for (let i = start; i <= end; i++) sum += block[i];
      count += block.length;
    }
    return sum;
  }

  _split(block) {
    const mid = Math.floor(block.length / 2);
    const newBlock = { arr: block.arr.splice(mid), sum: newBlock.arr.reduce((a,b)=>a+b,0) };
    block.sum = block.arr.reduce((a,b)=>a+b,0);
    const idx = this.blocks.indexOf(block);
    this.blocks.splice(idx + 1, 0, newBlock);
  }

  _merge(block) {
    const idx = this.blocks.indexOf(block);
    const neighbor = idx > 0 ? this.blocks[idx - 1] : this.blocks[idx + 1];
    const [small, big] = neighbor.length > block.length ? [block, neighbor] : [neighbor, block];
    big.arr.push(...small.arr);
    big.sum += small.sum;
    this.blocks.splice(this.blocks.indexOf(small), 1);
  }
}
```
